<title>JAPAN: Japan to keep measures to help small firms.</title>
<headline>Japan to keep measures to help small firms.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of International Trade and Industry will continue a cut in or exemption from interest payments for loans provided by government-affiliated financial institutions to small- and medium-sized companies, Trade Minister Shunpei Tsukahara told reporters on Friday.</p>
<p>The steps were introduced last October as temporary measures, effective only for a year, but the ministry had decided to maintain them for another year as the business environment remained difficult for small companies, Tsukahara said at a news conference.</p>
